<section class="page-head">
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="eyebrow">Performing</p>
    <h1>Three roles, one calling.</h1>
    <p class="lede">Adán performs as organist, harpsichordist, and conductor. The thread through all three is the music of the Church, and in particular the sacred music of Latin America.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="cards">
      <div class="card reveal">
        <h3>Organ</h3>
        <p>Recitals and residencies on instruments from parish lofts to concert halls. Bach and the German baroque, the French symphonists, Liszt, Messiaen, and living American composers. Second Prize at the International Liszt Organ Competition; a fellow of the Oregon Bach Festival Organ Institute under Paul Jacobs.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card reveal">
        <h3>Harpsichord &amp; early music</h3>
        <p>Continuo and solo work with Hortus Musicus, with a particular interest in the Spanish and Latin American baroque. In 2025 he directed the Padilla villancicos from the harpsichord, their first performance in three hundred years.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card reveal">
        <h3>Conducting</h3>
        <p>Choral and orchestral conducting, from the parish choirs and the youth orchestra he founded to guest engagements such as the Requiem for St. Oscar Romero at the Cathedral of Our Lady of the Angels. Conducting Fellow with the Kansas City Chorale.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

